WEBVTT

00:03.580 --> 00:06.030
<b>I hope we finish the day 
in a good position again.</b>

00:08.210 --> 00:09.870
<b>Oh, welcome back.</b>

00:09.870 --> 00:11.610
<b>The base over there is takeable.</b>

00:12.600 --> 00:15.470
<b>Should we divide up the 
spells that just dropped?</b>

00:15.470 --> 00:16.680
<b>Sounds good.</b>

00:16.680 --> 00:18.450
<b>I'll take Swordflash, then.</b>

00:18.450 --> 00:19.120
<b>Huh?</b>

00:19.120 --> 00:19.620
<b>Begin Battle</b>

00:19.620 --> 00:20.620
<b>Action Unavailable</b>

00:20.600 --> 00:22.820
<b>Huh? But where's the enemy?</b>

00:20.620 --> 00:20.750
<b>Action Unavailable</b>

00:20.750 --> 00:20.950
<b>Action Unavailable</b>

00:20.950 --> 00:21.040
<b>Action Unavailable</b>

00:21.040 --> 00:22.540
<b>Action Unavailable</b>

00:22.540 --> 00:22.710
<b>Action Unavailable</b>

00:22.710 --> 00:22.830
<b>Action Unavailable</b>

00:22.820 --> 00:24.290
<b>No one here has...</b>

00:22.830 --> 00:22.960
<b>Action Unavailable</b>

00:22.960 --> 00:24.290
<b>Action Unavailable</b>

00:24.290 --> 00:24.420
<b>Action Unavailable</b>

00:24.290 --> 00:25.950
<b>...accepted a battle?</b>

00:24.420 --> 00:24.500
<b>Action Unavailable</b>

00:24.500 --> 00:24.540
<b>Action Unavailable</b>

00:25.950 --> 00:27.880
<b>Huh? No way, a trap?</b>

00:28.350 --> 00:30.040
<b>Wait. But why?</b>

00:34.480 --> 00:36.050
<b>What the hell are you doing?</b>

00:41.290 --> 00:45.440
<b>Hey. Are we gonna start 
this game for real or what?</b>

02:16.990 --> 02:20.990
<b>Search</b>

02:17.490 --> 02:20.980
<b><i>Hey. Are we gonna start 
this game for real or what?</i></b>

02:21.410 --> 02:26.410
<b>Facing Off 
and Flushing Out</b>

02:21.430 --> 02:26.490
<b>This happened at the end of the second day.
For some reason, it isn't archived on Libra.</b>

02:26.490 --> 02:29.130
<b>A regular student saved the video.</b>

02:29.130 --> 02:32.870
<b>Really? Well, that explains 
the weird mood today.</b>

02:33.210 --> 02:37.120
<b>Guess this means Saionji isn't the only 
person the doppelgänger can impersonate.</b>

02:37.120 --> 02:40.850
<b><i>S-Something totally unprecedented
 is happening, meow!</i></b>

02:40.840 --> 02:45.100
<b>Special</b>

02:40.840 --> 02:45.100
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

02:40.840 --> 02:45.100
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

02:40.840 --> 02:45.100
<b>The Hotly Anticipated New Superstar Appears\h\h\h!</b>

02:42.040 --> 02:45.090
<b><i>Wait. This looks a little different 
from that other image.</i></b>

02:45.090 --> 02:48.150
<b><i>And why does Kazami 
sound like she's out of it?</i></b>

02:49.780 --> 02:52.850
<b>First, we need to figure out 
how this doppelgänger thing works.</b>

02:53.100 --> 02:56.120
<b>Right, yeah. I was wondering 
about that. What <i>is</i> she?</b>

02:56.790 --> 03:00.620
<b>She came in, guns blazing, 
saying she was the true Empress,</b>

03:00.620 --> 03:04.870
<b>but it looks like she can copy the 
appearance of anyone in ASTRAL.</b>

03:04.870 --> 03:08.750
<b>So, wait, she could turn into any of us, too?</b>

03:08.750 --> 03:09.520
<b>Hmph.</b>

03:09.520 --> 03:10.370
<b>What?</b>

03:10.660 --> 03:14.570
<b>Yes, but if we employ information-sensing
 abilities, we can prevent that.</b>

03:14.570 --> 03:18.380
<b>In other words, just don't give her
 any opportunity to replace us.</b>

03:18.630 --> 03:23.200
<b>We should try to always 
keep our teammates in sight.</b>

03:23.200 --> 03:26.380
<b>Inside the game, we should
move in pairs at a minimum.</b>

03:26.850 --> 03:27.640
<b>Got it?</b>

03:28.390 --> 03:29.610
<b>Sounds reasonable.</b>

03:29.970 --> 03:33.980
<b>As long as no one goes off alone and 
disappears, it shouldn't be a problem.</b>

03:39.040 --> 03:42.280
<b>Aha! Wicked Inferno Strike!</b>

03:43.780 --> 03:46.070
<b>Aw, I lost.</b>

03:46.070 --> 03:47.750
<b>It's two in the morning, you know.</b>

03:48.450 --> 03:50.670
<b>I was having so much fun, I couldn't help it.</b>

03:50.670 --> 03:53.230
<b>I got to play <i>all</i> day and night.</b>

03:53.230 --> 03:56.430
<b>I was bored before, 
but today was as fun as it gets!</b>

03:57.190 --> 03:58.360
<b><i>All day, too?</i></b>

03:59.050 --> 04:01.420
<b>What do you usually do about school?</b>

04:01.420 --> 04:06.450
<b>Huh? I don't go. If I went outside, 
I'd have to talk to all sorts of people.</b>

04:06.450 --> 04:09.290
<b>I just wanna do things that are fun!</b>

04:09.290 --> 04:11.420
<b>But you're okay talking to me?</b>

04:11.420 --> 04:15.640
<b>Yeah, of course! 
I think you're great, mister!</b>

04:22.070 --> 04:24.080
<b>You're falling asleep <i>there</i>?</b>

04:25.810 --> 04:27.580
<b><i>It's time I got going.</i></b>

04:35.280 --> 04:36.080
<b>Who is it?</b>

04:36.560 --> 04:38.340
<b>Your accomplice.</b>

04:38.340 --> 04:40.370
<b>Huh? G-Gimme ten minutes.</b>

04:40.370 --> 04:43.670
<b>T-Ten minutes? Are you kidding?</b>

04:43.670 --> 04:47.210
<b>Then, five. Give me five minutes.
 Wait out there for me.</b>

04:47.210 --> 04:48.790
<b>That's still too long!</b>

04:53.780 --> 04:54.820
<b>Come in.</b>

04:55.160 --> 04:56.300
<b>O-Okay.</b>

05:01.450 --> 05:04.890
<b>H-Hey, quit looking around, dummy.</b>

05:04.890 --> 05:06.100
<b>U-Uh, right.</b>

05:06.100 --> 05:08.860
<b>Th-That doesn't mean you should look at me.</b>

05:09.140 --> 05:11.130
<b>Then where am I supposed to look?</b>

05:11.130 --> 05:15.110
<b>Wh-Why don't you look out the window 
at all the lights? Aren't they pretty?</b>

05:16.010 --> 05:18.630
<b>If anyone saw me here, 
it'd be a huge scandal.</b>

05:19.230 --> 05:23.630
<b>"Passionate Love Between Seven Star Transfer
Student and Genius Princess Uncovered."</b>

05:24.180 --> 05:27.050
<b>"P-Passionate love"? Y-You dummy!</b>

05:27.050 --> 05:30.220
<b>I'm obviously out of your league!</b>

05:30.220 --> 05:33.900
<b>Can I at least sit down? 
There's something I wanna talk to you about.</b>

05:34.850 --> 05:36.640
<b>It's about the doppelgänger.</b>

05:37.360 --> 05:40.400
<b>Everything seems to be
 about her these days.</b>

05:41.210 --> 05:46.920
<b>It's such a pain, though. She gets all the 
attention because she looks just like me.</b>

05:46.920 --> 05:49.400
<b>And she's such a good actor. 
It pisses me off.</b>

05:49.700 --> 05:52.700
<b>Normally, you'd think 
people wouldn't stand for it.</b>

05:52.700 --> 05:56.940
<b>People are already calling her
 "Miss Hundred Faces."</b>

05:56.940 --> 06:01.420
<b>I bet people are gonna stop trusting 
their friends over the tiniest things now.</b>

06:01.690 --> 06:04.780
<b>Teams might even 
self-destruct over suspicions.</b>

06:04.780 --> 06:06.690
<b>Yeah, that doesn't seem impossible.</b>

06:06.900 --> 06:10.940
<b>The team likely to be most affected
 by this Miss Hundred Faces is Eimei.</b>

06:10.940 --> 06:15.790
<b>And, uh, actually, if I don't take out 
two other commanders today,</b>

06:15.790 --> 06:18.190
<b>I lose a bet with my teammate.</b>

06:18.190 --> 06:21.840
<b>W-Wait, how can you say 
that so casually? That's bad.</b>

06:21.840 --> 06:25.260
<b>Sorry. But it's not like 
I'm not prepared for it.</b>

06:25.260 --> 06:28.190
<b>Huh? You mean you've got a plan of some kind?</b>

06:28.190 --> 06:32.210
<b>Yeah. That's what I sneaked 
over here to talk to you about.</b>

06:33.070 --> 06:37.940
<b>A way to finish top of ASTRAL even after 
Miss Hundred Faces has shaken everything up.</b>

06:40.710 --> 06:42.670
<b>ASTRAL Third Day: Morning</b>

06:40.970 --> 06:42.820
<b>We need to take more bases.</b>

06:42.820 --> 06:45.590
<b>Then we should try going that way instead.</b>

06:45.590 --> 06:46.560
<b>Yeah, I guess so.</b>

06:46.910 --> 06:47.640
<b>Huh?</b>

06:47.640 --> 06:48.330
<b>What?</b>

06:54.580 --> 06:55.620
<b>What are you doing?</b>

06:55.620 --> 06:56.770
<b>Wait a minute!</b>

07:16.510 --> 07:18.990
<b>Hey, Nanase. You're walking too far ahead.</b>

07:18.990 --> 07:23.820
<b>You can still see me, can't you? I'm just 
leading the way 'cause I'm the best fighter.</b>

07:23.820 --> 07:28.260
<b>I can still see you right now, 
but you're being too careless.</b>

07:28.260 --> 07:32.180
<b>You just need to keep up! 
You're seriously pissing me off!</b>

07:29.460 --> 07:33.030
<b>Master, if you wish, I can intervene.</b>

07:32.180 --> 07:36.220
<b>I don't care if you're pissed off. If we don't 
follow the plan we talked about last night...</b>

07:33.030 --> 07:35.720
<b>Ah, no. I should do it myself.</b>

07:43.870 --> 07:45.110
<b>What <i>is</i> this?</b>

07:45.110 --> 07:48.640
<b><i>Hiro-kyun, it must be that 
super versatile ability, Blackout!</i></b>

07:48.990 --> 07:51.450
<b><i>This is bad! There's zero visibility!</i></b>

07:51.450 --> 07:53.450
<b><i>I won't know if someone gets replaced!</i></b>

07:53.450 --> 07:57.660
<b>Answer me, Nanase! What did you 
buy me for my birthday last year?</b>

07:58.220 --> 08:01.880
<b>Huh? I-I don't remember. 
Why ask me that now?</b>

08:01.880 --> 08:04.040
<b>Are you suggesting I'm Miss Hundred Faces?</b>

08:04.300 --> 08:06.040
<b>You could be, so answer!</b>

08:06.040 --> 08:10.540
<b>There's no way! But with the way you're 
talking, <i>you</i> might be Miss Hundred Faces.</b>

08:10.540 --> 08:12.960
<b><i>Oh, man, this is bad. What do I do now?</i></b>

08:21.120 --> 08:24.390
<b>Hey, Nanase, where are you going?
There's still the afternoon—</b>

08:23.990 --> 08:25.230
<b>I'm done!</b>

08:25.230 --> 08:26.890
<b>I'm tired of being a suspect.</b>

08:27.160 --> 08:29.390
<b>I'm not playing this afternoon.</b>

08:29.390 --> 08:30.410
<b>What?</b>

08:30.940 --> 08:32.160
<b>Wait, Nanase!</b>

08:35.840 --> 08:38.850
<b>Sorry. I need to go cool my head.</b>

08:39.260 --> 08:42.860
<b>There's a good chance Nanase and I 
won't be able to play this afternoon.</b>

08:42.860 --> 08:46.370
<b>No, we probably shouldn't 
play in the first place.</b>

08:46.700 --> 08:50.870
<b>Enomoto-sama, if you back out now, 
what happens to your leadership bet?</b>

08:51.150 --> 08:52.710
<b>Oh, you're right.</b>

08:52.710 --> 08:57.310
<b>Let's just say I was never cut out
to be the commander to begin with.</b>

08:59.150 --> 09:03.640
<b>Man, those two. I wish they 
could be a bit more easygoing.</b>

09:08.650 --> 09:10.440
<b>ASTRAL Third Day: Afternoon</b>

09:12.150 --> 09:15.150
<b>Looks like Mya-chan and 
the council prez are no-shows.</b>

09:15.400 --> 09:18.190
<b>Players cannot join a 
session once it is underway,</b>

09:18.190 --> 09:21.160
<b>so the earliest they will be 
back is tomorrow morning.</b>

09:21.940 --> 09:23.510
<b>Yeah. It is what it is.</b>

09:23.510 --> 09:26.790
<b>Let's fight our way through 
this afternoon like we discussed.</b>

09:27.500 --> 09:30.800
<b><i>Hiro-kyun, I know you only just started,
 but you're surrounded!</i></b>

09:32.640 --> 09:36.000
<b>Himeji! Akizuki! Two teams 
inbound from the north and south!</b>

09:36.000 --> 09:37.570
<b>At this rate, we'll be flanked!</b>

09:37.570 --> 09:38.590
<b>Huh?</b>

09:38.890 --> 09:42.090
<b>I bet the person who used 
Blackout is on one of those teams.</b>

09:42.090 --> 09:47.810
<b>Aw! Just when it was starting to feel
like a date, it's all ruined! Jeez.</b>

09:47.810 --> 09:53.240
<b>I do not mind at all if that feeling is ruined, 
but being flanked spells trouble for us.</b>

09:53.240 --> 09:56.610
<b>If their whole goal was to force out
Mya-chan and the prez,</b>

09:56.610 --> 09:58.610
<b>they'll probably attack right away.</b>

09:58.610 --> 10:00.180
<b>Yeah, makes sense.</b>

10:00.830 --> 10:04.740
<b>Is our plan really going to work?</b>

10:04.740 --> 10:07.750
<b>I know you and I are the most
 powerful power couple ever,</b>

10:07.750 --> 10:10.550
<b>and as third wheels go,
 Maid-chan's pretty useful...</b>

10:10.920 --> 10:12.550
<b>But wouldn't it be better to run?</b>

10:12.550 --> 10:17.800
<b>I shall teach you who the "third wheel" is
 soon enough, but I have doubts myself.</b>

10:17.800 --> 10:22.450
<b>Well, then, maybe we should try and
 squeeze a little more out of our secret plan.</b>

10:30.610 --> 10:34.320
<b>It's been two days since I met you, 
Mr. "Strongest on Academy Island."</b>

10:34.320 --> 10:36.450
<b><i>Why'd it have to be her?</i></b>

10:36.850 --> 10:41.060
<b>Sorry that we're short two. 
I wanted to face you with a full team.</b>

10:41.060 --> 10:46.720
<b>That's no problem. After all, I'm the one 
who made sure they'd be out of the picture.</b>

10:46.720 --> 10:51.330
<b>Hah. You even admit it? So that whole
 "straight arrow" thing was just an act?</b>

10:51.330 --> 10:53.340
<b>It's time to put an end to this.</b>

10:53.600 --> 10:56.500
<b>Master, I will leave her to you.</b>

10:58.040 --> 10:59.740
<b>Huh? T-Two of them?</b>

10:59.740 --> 11:01.680
<b>Th-This is bad! Let's split!</b>

11:03.540 --> 11:05.190
<b>Are you in your right mind?</b>

11:05.590 --> 11:07.950
<b>You plan to face me alone?</b>

11:09.010 --> 11:12.620
<b>Not another step! 
There's one of you and five of us.</b>

11:12.620 --> 11:15.300
<b>We have a larger number of spells than you.</b>

11:15.300 --> 11:19.150
<b>Even someone like you can't beat those odds.</b>

11:20.650 --> 11:22.160
<b>Oh, I wouldn't say that.</b>

11:22.160 --> 11:24.660
<b></b>Movement Value

11:22.160 --> 11:24.740
<b>Team
Slot</b>

11:22.160 --> 11:24.740
<b>Ability</b>

11:22.160 --> 11:24.740
<b>Temporary 
Alliance</b>

11:22.160 --> 11:24.740
<b>Occupy</b>

11:22.160 --> 11:25.660
<b>I'm more than a match for all five of you.</b>

11:24.660 --> 11:24.830
<b></b>Movement Value

11:24.830 --> 11:24.910
<b></b>Movement Value

11:24.830 --> 11:26.040
<b>Predict</b>

11:24.830 --> 11:26.040
<b>Movement</b>

11:24.830 --> 11:26.040
<b>Wings</b>

11:24.830 --> 11:26.040
<b>Information</b>

11:24.830 --> 11:26.040
<b>Control EX</b>

11:24.910 --> 11:26.030
<b></b>Movement Value

11:29.300 --> 11:30.710
<b>Where did that come from?</b>

11:42.380 --> 11:43.880
<b>One down.</b>

11:43.880 --> 11:47.340
<b>Looks like Magic Blast worked.
 Was she your spy?</b>

11:48.790 --> 11:50.360
<b>How dare you!</b>

11:52.240 --> 11:54.710
<b>I have returned, Master.</b>

11:54.710 --> 11:56.720
<b>Yeah. Good work, Himeji.</b>

11:56.720 --> 11:59.370
<b><i>Teehee. That worked a treat!</i></b>

11:59.370 --> 12:03.360
<b><i>Shirayuki-chan pretended to go with Noa 
and caught the Tsuyuri team off guard.</i></b>

12:04.380 --> 12:08.070
<b><i>Question is, did that disrupt
 the conditions for One-Shot Kill?</i></b>

12:10.290 --> 12:11.230
<b>Master!</b>

12:16.620 --> 12:19.630
<b>I guess that Barrier kept me
 from finishing you off.</b>

12:20.230 --> 12:23.760
<b>It still wiped out most 
of your life points. Damn it.</b>

12:23.760 --> 12:24.480
<b>Let's retreat.</b>

12:24.480 --> 12:25.390
<b>Right!</b>

12:30.260 --> 12:31.550
<b>What's this?</b>

12:33.020 --> 12:34.520
<b>Such insolence!</b>

12:34.520 --> 12:35.980
<b></b>Spell

12:34.520 --> 12:38.980
<b>You're using a Counteract spell and trying 
to turn the battlefield to your advantage?</b>

12:38.980 --> 12:40.960
<b>Yeah, do you think?</b>

12:41.310 --> 12:44.580
<b><i>The misdirection's working.
 But this is bad.</i></b>

12:44.580 --> 12:47.310
<b><i>Kururugi's One-Shot Kill 
isn't disarmed yet.</i></b>

12:47.780 --> 12:48.980
<b>Master.</b>

12:49.750 --> 12:51.910
<b>I have an idea.</b>

12:51.910 --> 12:55.080
<b>If it works, we will eliminate 
another Tsuyuri member.</b>

12:55.840 --> 12:58.010
<b>But I will have to risk my life.</b>

12:58.010 --> 13:01.450
<b>Knowing that, may I ask
 you to please trust me?</b>

13:01.450 --> 13:05.770
<b>Of course you can. I've never 
<i>not</i> trusted you. Not even once.</b>

13:06.950 --> 13:09.140
<b>Okay. Thank you very much.</b>

13:11.800 --> 13:13.950
<b>I will not allow you to go any further.</b>

13:13.950 --> 13:14.730
<b>Himeji?</b>

13:16.480 --> 13:19.980
<b>Oh? Don't tell me you're going 
to try the same thing again?</b>

13:19.980 --> 13:23.500
<b>If that is what you think, then why not
 make the first move yourself?</b>

13:23.500 --> 13:25.980
<b>I see how it is. Then I shall.</b>

13:34.830 --> 13:36.470
<b>Damn you! What did you do?</b>

13:36.830 --> 13:38.580
<b>I used Numerical Adjustment.</b>

13:39.400 --> 13:40.310
<b>Ridiculous!</b>

13:40.550 --> 13:44.770
<b>Attack spells are programmed to 
deal damage to the targeted player.</b>

13:45.410 --> 13:50.300
<b>But by recalculating the target and timing,
 I can redirect the attack.</b>

13:50.300 --> 13:53.020
<b><b>Ability</b></b>

13:50.600 --> 13:53.000
<b><i>She managed to calculate
 all that in seconds?</i></b>

13:53.000 --> 13:56.770
<b><i>W-Wow. She isn't the 
Company's leader for nothing.</i></b>

13:56.770 --> 13:59.780
<b>D-Damn you. What are you?</b>

14:00.620 --> 14:02.420
<b>I am a maid.</b>

14:02.420 --> 14:09.840
<b>The personal maid of Academy Island's 
strongest student, Shinohara Hiroto-sama.</b>

14:14.080 --> 14:17.550
<b><i>This battle's more difficult than 
I imagined, but I'm not worried.</i></b>

14:18.120 --> 14:20.330
<b><i>I'm making them use up their spells.</i></b>

14:25.670 --> 14:28.460
<b>Impossible. When did they use Trap?</b>

14:28.460 --> 14:30.180
<b>That's three down.</b>

14:30.180 --> 14:35.140
<b>Our Little Devil has a knack for 
reading people's plans and moves.</b>

14:35.740 --> 14:39.450
<b>She's been dropping those Traps she loves
 all around during the fight.</b>

14:42.080 --> 14:46.740
<b>I see now. You were planning this all along
 when you went after Kagurazuki.</b>

14:46.740 --> 14:49.070
<b>You don't disappoint,
Mr. "Strongest on Academy Island."</b>

14:49.340 --> 14:52.740
<b>However, your plan has one fatal flaw.</b>

14:52.740 --> 14:53.730
<b>Flaw?</b>

14:54.170 --> 14:57.740
<b>You have clearly used far 
too many Counteract spells.</b>

14:58.170 --> 15:00.860
<b>I bet you didn't prepare 
any real attack spells.</b>

15:01.120 --> 15:03.360
<b>Oh, yeah? You wouldn't know how many—</b>

15:03.360 --> 15:04.900
<b>You used 35.</b>

15:05.250 --> 15:08.170
<b>You've used Counteract 35 times.</b>

15:08.170 --> 15:10.430
<b>Counting the Magic Blast at the start,</b>

15:10.430 --> 15:14.000
<b>there shouldn't be a single spell 
left in your personal slots.</b>

15:14.560 --> 15:18.010
<b><i>Seriously? She was able 
to count during all that?</i></b>

15:19.060 --> 15:23.060
<b>You may have forgotten, 
but Master still has me by his side.</b>

15:23.060 --> 15:26.270
<b>You will not get to him 
without going through his maid first.</b>

15:33.500 --> 15:34.240
<b>Himeji!</b>

15:35.240 --> 15:37.240
<b>Medusa's
Magic Eye</b>

15:35.240 --> 15:37.240
<b></b>Ability

15:35.490 --> 15:37.260
<b>Medusa's Magic Eye.</b>

15:37.600 --> 15:41.000
<b>It's an ability that prevents an
opponent from moving for one minute.</b>

15:41.000 --> 15:42.750
<b>That sure sounds handy.</b>

15:42.750 --> 15:45.750
<b>With this, our victory is ensured.</b>

15:45.750 --> 15:51.510
<b>Are you sure? Doesn't One-Shot Kill 
require your teammates' cooperation?</b>

15:52.060 --> 15:58.040
<b>Actually, One-Shot Kill only produces 
its greatest effect when I'm fighting alone.</b>

15:58.040 --> 15:58.510
<b>Huh?</b>

15:58.870 --> 16:01.760
<b>But that was much too sad.</b>

16:02.310 --> 16:06.530
<b>I used an ability to overwrite and 
restrict its conditions for activation,</b>

16:07.300 --> 16:10.410
<b>so that I would not be able 
to use it without allies.</b>

16:10.890 --> 16:13.270
<b>But now, I must undo that restriction.</b>

16:14.640 --> 16:17.210
<b>Please forgive my cowardice.</b>

16:19.250 --> 16:20.070
<b>Wha...</b>

16:20.070 --> 16:23.050
<b>From the beginning, 
I was always stronger alone.</b>

16:23.530 --> 16:27.210
<b>Now you will regret ever belittling us.</b>

16:31.310 --> 16:32.880
<b>One-Shot Kill!</b>

16:40.350 --> 16:41.340
<b>Wha...</b>

16:44.220 --> 16:48.220
<b>Wh-What's going on? 
Your slots should be empty by now!</b>

16:49.460 --> 16:53.980
<b>Yeah, you <i>could</i> say I changed a bunch 
of spaces to green, but that would be...</b>

16:54.530 --> 16:56.210
<b>your misunderstanding.</b>

16:56.840 --> 16:57.940
<b>It can't be!</b>

16:58.230 --> 16:59.950
<b>Black Wings.</b>

17:00.380 --> 17:04.700
<b>It's an ability that lets me control visual 
effects. I just changed the way they looked.</b>

17:04.710 --> 17:08.460
<b></b>Spell

17:05.120 --> 17:08.470
<b>I've barely used what's in 
my personal slots at all.</b>

17:14.720 --> 17:17.220
<b>Operation Unavailable</b>

17:14.720 --> 17:17.220
<b>Operation Unavailable</b>

17:14.720 --> 17:17.220
<b>Freeze Time
Activated</b>

17:14.720 --> 17:17.220
<b>Freeze Time
Activated</b>

17:15.060 --> 17:16.750
<b>What's happening? Damn it!</b>

17:17.210 --> 17:18.750
<b>Electronic Interference.</b>

17:17.220 --> 17:20.220
<b>Electronic
Interference</b>

17:17.220 --> 17:20.220
<b></b>Ability

17:18.750 --> 17:20.210
<b>My trump card.</b>

17:20.470 --> 17:25.090
<b>For Tsuyuri's honor as well as my own, 
I cannot allow myself to be defeated here.</b>

17:25.770 --> 17:27.690
<b>Huh? Hey!</b>

17:32.140 --> 17:34.450
<b>Well done, Master.</b>

17:34.450 --> 17:35.560
<b>Himeji.</b>

17:35.560 --> 17:38.960
<b>Kururugi-sama is quite 
adept in battle, isn't she?</b>

17:38.960 --> 17:41.660
<b>Her intuition and 
resourcefulness are top-level.</b>

17:42.080 --> 17:45.780
<b>But wasn't it a little strange? 
That Electronic Interference, I mean.</b>

17:45.780 --> 17:49.670
<b>If she'd timed an attack spell with it,
 she could have taken me out.</b>

17:49.670 --> 17:53.120
<b>It does seem that way. 
Perhaps she had a reason not to.</b>

17:53.120 --> 17:55.420
<b>Hiroto-kun!</b>

17:57.710 --> 18:02.480
<b>I took care of those other two.
 Didn't I do good?</b>

18:02.480 --> 18:04.040
<b>Y-Yeah.</b>

18:04.570 --> 18:07.450
<b>Thanks a lot. I survived thanks to you.</b>

18:07.770 --> 18:09.100
<b>All right!</b>

18:09.100 --> 18:12.050
<b>But isn't it kind of weird?</b>

18:12.050 --> 18:14.510
<b>Even though we wiped out Kagurazuki,</b>

18:14.510 --> 18:17.300
<b>Eimei's area hasn't 
increased by even one space.</b>

18:20.080 --> 18:22.630
<b>You're right. That's strange.</b>

18:23.430 --> 18:26.900
<b>Now that I think of it, 
those two said something weird.</b>

18:26.900 --> 18:30.140
<b>Something about "working under
 Miss Hundred Faces' umbrella."</b>

18:30.890 --> 18:32.440
<b><i>What could that mean?</i></b>

18:32.440 --> 18:35.950
<b><i>With all this happening, 
I don't think it's unrelated.</i></b>

18:35.950 --> 18:38.630
<b><i>That guy must be plotting 
something after all.</i></b>

18:39.020 --> 18:42.350
<b><i>At this point, I've only got 
one shot. It's all or nothing.</i></b>

18:42.350 --> 18:46.400
<b>Listen up, you two. Trust me
 and listen to what I have to say.</b>

18:49.260 --> 18:51.480
<b>I'm really, really sorry.</b>

18:51.910 --> 18:54.470
<b>I watched the live broadcast. So did Nanase.</b>

18:54.900 --> 18:59.230
<b>Thanks to my arrogance, your name 
and Eimei's got dragged through the mud.</b>

18:59.940 --> 19:02.960
<b>Enomoto, tell me the truth.</b>

19:02.960 --> 19:06.160
<b>Did you really suspect that 
Asamiya was Miss Hundred Faces?</b>

19:07.360 --> 19:10.910
<b>No, I just said it to make her mad.</b>

19:11.350 --> 19:15.370
<b>She's foolish, but she's honest and pure. 
She doesn't respond well to cruelty.</b>

19:15.370 --> 19:18.590
<b>If she'd stayed in the game, 
she would've fallen apart.</b>

19:18.900 --> 19:20.920
<b>I wanted to make sure that didn't—</b>

19:20.920 --> 19:22.920
<b>Why are you looking at me like that?</b>

19:22.920 --> 19:26.930
<b>Huh? Oh, uh, it's like you just 
started opening up all of a sudden.</b>

19:28.120 --> 19:30.170
<b>It's something that's always on my mind,</b>

19:30.520 --> 19:33.180
<b>but I don't want to complicate things,
 so I keep my mouth shut.</b>

19:38.400 --> 19:42.200
<b>S-Sorry, Shino! I wasn't trying 
to eavesdrop, I promise!</b>

19:42.200 --> 19:44.380
<b>How much did you hear, Nanase?</b>

19:44.380 --> 19:47.210
<b>Depending on your answer, 
I may have to erase your memory!</b>

19:47.210 --> 19:49.440
<b>Um, I know, I know!</b>

19:49.440 --> 19:52.470
<b>"I totally have the hots for Nanase." 
It was around that part.</b>

19:52.940 --> 19:55.080
<b>I never said anything like that!</b>

19:55.080 --> 19:57.470
<b>And that's not how I talk anyway!</b>

19:57.470 --> 20:00.400
<b>Then, "She's always on my mind."</b>

20:00.400 --> 20:01.470
<b>I didn't say that!</b>

20:01.470 --> 20:04.240
<b>Y-You totally <i>did</i> say that!</b>

20:04.670 --> 20:07.480
<b>I noticed something when 
I watched the video on Libra.</b>

20:08.210 --> 20:10.670
<b>When we were talking to 
the Ibara Academy guys,</b>

20:10.670 --> 20:13.140
<b>one of them was about 
to use a Magic Blast spell.</b>

20:13.500 --> 20:16.150
<b>I noticed when I slowed it 
down to one-tenth speed.</b>

20:17.250 --> 20:19.140
<b>That's the guy Asamiya attacked.</b>

20:19.520 --> 20:21.130
<b>Is that what happened?</b>

20:21.130 --> 20:25.130
<b>So you weren't just charging ahead? 
You had a reason for doing that?</b>

20:25.130 --> 20:28.390
<b>I told you, I'm trying to do
 my part for everyone.</b>

20:28.390 --> 20:33.020
<b>Shino's totally reliable, 
Noa's cute and super clever,</b>

20:33.020 --> 20:35.420
<b>Yuki-rin's also cute and super smart,</b>

20:35.420 --> 20:38.910
<b>and you, Shinji... 
Well, I wouldn't call you cute,</b>

20:38.910 --> 20:41.610
<b>but you do help hold the team together.</b>

20:42.140 --> 20:44.920
<b>All I can do is fight.</b>

20:44.920 --> 20:47.630
<b>That's why you reacted 
so abnormally quickly?</b>

20:47.630 --> 20:50.190
<b>I had to. I saw it going down.</b>

20:50.460 --> 20:53.490
<b>But, I mean, isn't it all over now?</b>

20:53.490 --> 20:57.400
<b>Since we don't have any area or spells,
 our popularity's dropping,</b>

20:57.400 --> 20:59.690
<b>and Shino was eliminated.</b>

20:59.690 --> 21:03.450
<b>Huh? I didn't know that. 
Shinohara was eliminated?</b>

21:03.840 --> 21:07.440
<b>Shino was eliminated from 
ASTRAL at the end of the day.</b>

21:07.810 --> 21:10.180
<b>And he did it to himself.</b>

21:10.610 --> 21:14.690
<b>Listen up, you two. Trust me 
and listen to what I have to say.</b>

21:17.400 --> 21:18.340
<b>Huh?</b>

21:25.310 --> 21:26.980
<b>Why would you do that?!</b>

21:27.400 --> 21:30.480
<b>Did you do it just to 
win your bet with me?</b>

21:31.190 --> 21:35.940
<b>Yeah, the bet was one reason,
 but not the only one.</b>

21:35.940 --> 21:40.120
<b>Will you being eliminated 
help Eimei win somehow?</b>

21:41.210 --> 21:44.690
<b>Miss Hundred Faces has 
turned ASTRAL upside-down.</b>

21:44.690 --> 21:47.450
<b>She now has groups 
working under her "umbrella,"</b>

21:47.450 --> 21:50.190
<b>and among her opponents, 
we're bottom of the pile.</b>

21:50.590 --> 21:52.480
<b>We can't win if we play it by the book.</b>

21:54.080 --> 21:55.620
<b>But don't worry.</b>

21:56.570 --> 21:57.710
<b>Everything's still...</b>

21:58.610 --> 22:00.230
<b>going according to plan.</b>

22:00.500 --> 22:02.000
<b>Third Day: Finished</b>

22:02.000 --> 22:03.550
<b>Team with the most held areas:
 District 12's Seijo Academy</b>

22:02.000 --> 22:03.550
<b>spaces</b>

22:03.550 --> 22:05.050
<b>Team with the most supporting votes:
 District 12's Seijo Academy</b>

22:05.050 --> 22:06.550
<b>Special Announcement</b>

22:06.550 --> 22:08.050
<b>Eimei Academy's</b>

22:06.550 --> 22:08.050
<b>Shinohara Hiroto</b>

22:08.050 --> 22:10.010
<b>Eliminated</b>
